-A spoken owner line also carries `floor` (`speaking`/`done`) and, when the clean-up changed it, `raw` (what Whisper heard). `quiet` (the owner went quiet for `ms`) and `skip` (a fast reply that said nothing) are never drawn.
+A spoken owner line also carries `floor` (`speaking`/`done`). `quiet` (the owner went quiet for `ms`) and `skip` (a fast reply that said nothing) are never drawn.
+
+**Not on the chat line (chat-live, 2026-10-25):** `raw` (what Whisper heard, when clean-up changed it) and `cues` (the mic's pause/speaking timing) are still accepted params of `POST /api/session/say` (below), but neither is stored on the chat line any more. `raw` is held in memory for the whole Prompt it belongs to and written ONCE, on a `{<prompt id>: {raw: {push: [...]}}}` line, when that Prompt closes — never once per chunk. `cues` is simply dropped: nothing reads it back off a session's chat line (only the unrelated page-assistant's own `prompts.jsonl` reads its own `cues`, a different log entirely). Measured on a real session: this cut raw+cues bytes from 25% of the file to 11%.
 
 `at` carries milliseconds, so two lines said in the same second never share one, and `re` always names exactly one owner line. `backing` maps the session to the Claude sessions behind it: `claude --resume <uuid>` reopens either one. When the assistants are respawned, a new `backing` line is written, and the latest one wins.
 
